        '[{"type":"text","value":"Managers"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option A Solution: Number of Managers working in the Company: In 1995 = 760. In 2000 = (760 + 280 + 179 + 148 + 160 + 193) - (120 + 92 + 88 + 72 + 96) = 1252. Therefore, Percentage increase in the number of Managers = [ x 100]% = 64.74% Number of Technicians working in the Company: In 1995 = 1200. In 2000 = (1200 + 272 + 240 + 236 + 256 + 288) - (120 + 128 + 96 + 100 + 112) = 1936. Therefore Percentage increase in the number of Technicians = [ x 100]% = 61.33% Number of Operators working in the Company: In 1995 = 880. In 2000 = (880 + 256 + 240 + 208 + 192 + 248) - (104 + 120 + 100 + 112 + 144) = 1444. Therefore Percentage increase in the number of Operators = [ x 100]% = 64.09% Number of Accountants working in the Company: In 1995 = 1160. In 2000 = (1160 + 200 + 224 + 248 + 272 + 260) - (100 + 104 + 96 + 88 + 92) = 1884. Therefore Percentage increase in the number of Accountants = [ x 100]% = 62.41% Number of Peons working in the Company: In 1995 = 820. In 2000 = (820 + 184 + 152 + 196 + 224 + 200) - (96 + 88 + 80 + 120 + 104) = 1288. Therefore Percentage increase in the number of Peons = [ x 100]% = 57.07% Clearly, the percentage increase is maximum in case of Managers."}]',
