        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option C Solution: Amount received from Company P after one year (i.e., in 199) on investing Rs. 12 lakhs in it = Rs. [12 + (8% of 12)] lakhs = Rs. 12.96 lakhs. Amount received from Company P after one year on investing Rs. 12.96 lakhs in the year 1999 = Rs. [12.96 + (10% of 12.96)] lakhs = Rs. 14.256. Appreciation received on investment during the period of two years = Rs. (14.256 - 12) lakhs = Rs. 2.256 lakhs = Rs. 2,25,600."}]',
