        '[{"type":"text","value":"Any law can be implemented in Jammu and Kashmir only if there is support from the state legislature."}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option C Solution: Refer to, “the amending provision of Article 368 says no Constitutional amendments have effect in relation to J&K unless applied by Order of the President under Article 370 that requires the concurrence of the State’s legislature and ratification by its Constituent Assembly.” It is stated in the passage that the Article 368 of the Indian Constitution is regarding the amendment of any law in the country. Any law will only be applicable in Jammu and Kashmir if the state legislature also accepts the same. The Presidential Order should also be in force regarding this. Among the given options, we can see that Option C gives us the correct information regarding the Article 368 of the Indian Constitution whereas the rest can be eliminated from consideration as they do not follow from the passage. This makes Option C the correct choice among the given options."}]',
