        '[{"type":"text","value":"900"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option A Solution: In this type of question, We need to find out the LCM of the given numbers. LCM of 12, 15, 18 and 20; 12=2×2×3; 15=3×5; 18=2×3×3; 20=2×2×5; Hence, LCM = 2×2×3×5×3 Since, the soldiers are in the form of a solid square. Hence, LCM must be a perfect square. To make the LCM a perfect square, We have to multiply it by 5, hence, The required number of soldiers = 2×2×3×3×5×5 = 900"}]',
