        1144,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Find the least number which will leaves remainder 5 when divided by 8, 12, 16 and 20."}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"240"}],[{"type":"text","value":"245"}],[{"type":"text","value":"265"}],[{"type":"text","value":"235"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"245"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: We have to find the Least number, therefore we find out the LCM of 8, 12, 16 and 20. 8 = 2 × 2 × 2; 12 = 2 × 2 × 3; 16 = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2; 20 = 2 × 2 × 5; LCM = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 3 × 5 = 240; This is the least number which is exactly divisible by 8, 12, 16 and 20 Thus, Required number which leaves remainder 5 is, 240 + 5 = 245"}]',
