    (
        1145,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"After the division of a number successively by 3, 4 and 7, the remainder obtained is 2, 1 and 4 respectively. What will be remainder if 84 divide the same number?"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"80"}],[{"type":"text","value":"75"}],[{"type":"text","value":"42"}],[{"type":"text","value":"53"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"53"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option D Solution: As the Number gives a remainder of 4 when it is divided by 7, then the number must be in form of (7x + 4) The same gives remainder 1 when it is divided 4, so the number must be in the form of {4 × (7x + 4) + 1} Also, the number when divided by 3 gives remainder 2, thus number must be in form of [3 × {4 × (7x + 4) + 1} + 2] Now, On simplifying, [3 × {4 × (7x + 4) + 1} + 2] = 84x + 53 We get the final number 53 more than a multiple of 84 Hence, if the number is divided by 84, The remainder will be 53"}]',
        4,
        25,
