    (
        1165,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"The greatest number which will divides: 4003, 4126 and 4249, leaving the same remainder in each case:"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"43"}],[{"type":"text","value":"41"}],[{"type":"text","value":"45"}],[{"type":"text","value":"None of these"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"41"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: Rule- Greatest number with which if we divide P, Q, R and it leaves same remainder in each case. Number is of form = HCF of (P - Q), (P - R) Therefore, HCF of (4126 - 4003), (4249 - 4003) = HCF of 123, 246 = 41.[Taken for Positive result]. Detailed Explanation: The numbers can be written as, 4003 = AX + P where P = Remainder 4126 = BX + P 4249 = CX + P (B - A) × X = 123 (C - B) × X = 246 Thus the X is factor of 123 and 246"}]',
