    (
        1169,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Two poles of heights 6m and 11m stand vertically on a plane ground. If the distance between their feet is 12m , what is the distance between their tops?"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"13m"}],[{"type":"text","value":"14m"}],[{"type":"text","value":"15m"}],[{"type":"text","value":"12.8m"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"13m"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option A Solution: Let AB and CD be the poles such that AB = 6 m, CD = 11 m and BD = 12m Draw AE ⊥ CD . Then , AE = BD = 12m CE = CD - DE = CD - AB = (11 - 6) m = 5 m. from right AEC, we have AC2 = AE2 + CE2 = (12)2 + 52 = (114 + 25) = 169. ⇒ Ac = √169 = 13m ∴ Distance between their tops= 13 m"},{"type":"image","value":"images/exp31_0.png"}]',
