        '[{"type":"text","value":"16"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option C Solution: Let N be the number that gives Q as quotient and 15 as the remainder when divided by d. Thus, d > 15 N = dQ+ 15 10N = 10(dQ)+ 144 + 6 clearly, d is a multiple of 144 which are: 2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 12, 16, 18, 24, and so on. The least possible value of d is 16. (d > 15)"}]',
