        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: It is given that 708x6y8z9 is divisible by 99. Thus, 708x6y8z9 is divisible by both 11 and 9 For divisibility by 9, the sum of digits is divisible by 9 (7+0+8+x+6+y+8+z+9 = 38+x+y+z. We get 2 as the remainder when 389. Thus, 2+x+y+z must be divisible by 9) Possible values of (z+y+x) = 7,16,25, etc. For divisibility by 11, the difference of sum of digits at odd and even place is divisible by 11 (i.e. in 708x6y8z9 : (9 + 8 + 6 + 8 + 7 ) - (z + y + x + 0) = 38 - ( z + y + x) is divisible by 11 ) Possible values of (z+y+x) =38,5,16 etc."}]',
