    (
        1211,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"If average weight of a family is ‘y’ kg. If a guest weighing 30 kg arrives then the average weight is increases by 1 kg. If the weight of this guest had been 18 kg then the average weight of the family would have decreased by 1 kg. Find ‘y’."}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"28"}],[{"type":"text","value":"24"}],[{"type":"text","value":"30"}],[{"type":"text","value":"22"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"24"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: Let the number of family members be x. Therefore, the total weight = xy Equation in the 1st scenario: (x + 1) (y + 1) = xy + 30 xy + x + y + 1 = xy + 30 x + y = 29 .....(i) Equation in the 2nd scenario: (x + 1) (y – 1) = xy + 18 xy + y – x – 1 = xy + 18 y - x = 19 ....(ii) Solving equations (i) and (ii), we get 2y = 48, Therefore, y = 24."}]',
