        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option A Solution: Narayan''s saving and rent = 1000 + 1800 = Rs. 2800 Let his monthly income be Rs. 100 30% of his income he spent on education i.e. Rs. 30 Remaining = 100 - 30 = 70 50% of remaining on food = =Rs. 35 Now, that 35 must be equal to his saving and rent i.e. 35 = 2800 then, 1 = 100 = = Rs. 8000 So, his income = Rs. 8000"}]',
