    (
        1240,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"A clock is set right at 12 noon on Monday. It losses % on the correct time in the first week but gains % on the true time during the second week. The time shown on Monday after two weeks will be"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"12 : 25 : 12"}],[{"type":"text","value":"11 : 34 : 48"}],[{"type":"text","value":"12 : 50 : 24"}],[{"type":"text","value":"12 : 24 : 16"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"11 : 34 : 48"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: Time lost over two weeks = 25% a week time(given that % clock loses in first week and in the second week it gains % on true time) A week = 168 hours Hence, clock lost = 0.42 hours = 25.2 minutes or 25 minute 12 seconds Thus, correct time = 11 : 34 : 48"}]',
