    (
        1242,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"A shepherd had n goats in the year 2000. In 2001 the no. of goats increased by 40%. In 2002 the no. of goats declined to 70%. In 2003 the no. of goats grew up 30%. In 2004, he sold 10% goats and then he had only 34,398 goats. The percentage increase of the no. of goats in this duration was :"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"16.66%"}],[{"type":"text","value":"14.66%"}],[{"type":"text","value":"11.33%"}],[{"type":"text","value":"20%"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"14.66%"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: There is no need of the number of goats given i.e. 34,398. Initially, let there be 100 goats. Then 100 == 40% ↑==> 140 == 30%↓(declined to 70%) ==> 98 == 30%↑ ==> 127.4 == 10%↓(sold) ==> 114.66 Hence, % increase = 14.66% [As 100 becomes 114.66]"}]',
