        '[{"type":"text","value":"70%"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option D Solution: Let the fixed part be x and the variable part be y Total salary = x + y Variable salary after first increment = (100 + 50) % of y = 1.5y Variable salary after second increment = (100 + 33.33) % of 1.5y = (4/3) × 1.5y = 2y Total salary after two increments = x + 2y The new salary is 30% more than the previous salary, ⇒ (100 + 30)% of (x + y) = x + 2y ⇒ 1.3x + 1.3y = x + 2y ⇒ 0.3x = 0.7y ⇒ = Let x be 7 units and y be 3 units Total salary = x + y = 10 units Percentage of constant salary = ( ) × 100 = 70%"}]',
