        1292,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"A shopkeeper buys some quantity of apples for Rs 6800. Out of all the apples, 20 kg were found bad condition and he had to sell them at 20% loss. To get a total profit of 20% the remaining apples have to be sold at 30% profit. What is the cost price of apples per kg? (in Rs)"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"34"}],[{"type":"text","value":"68"}],[{"type":"text","value":"17"}],[{"type":"text","value":"100"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"68"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: Let the amount of remaining apple be x and cost price be Rs y/kg 20% loss, SP = y × (100 – 20)/100 = 0.8y 30% profit, SP = 1.3y 20% profit, SP = 1.2y Total profit = Sum of profits by selling bad and good apples ⇒ (x + 20) × 1.2y = (x × 1.3y + 20 × 0.8y)/y ⇒ 1.2x + 24 = 1.3x + 16 ⇒ 8 = 0.1x ∴ x = 80 kg Total amount of apples = x + 20 = 100 kg ⇒ Cost of 1 kg of apple = Rs 6800/100 = Rs 68/kg"}]',
