    (
        1297,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"During a sale, a trader reduced the selling price of a motor car by offering a 20% discount. In this process, he incurred a loss of 8%. What would have been his profit percent, if he had instead offered a 12% discount?"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"1.2%"}],[{"type":"text","value":"3.4%"}],[{"type":"text","value":"3%"}],[{"type":"text","value":"2.5%"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"1.2%"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option A Solution: Let, the CP of the motor car be Rs 100 SP = 100 - (8% of 100) ⇒ 100 - ( ) × 8 = (100 - 8) = Rs. 92 Now, he gives a 20% discount on MRP 80% of MRP = Rs 92 MRP = ( ) × 100 = Rs 115 If he had offered a discount of only 12% Then, SP = 115 - (12% of 115) ⇒ 115 - ( ) × 12 ⇒ (115 - 13.8) = Rs. 101.2 Hence, profit = (101.2 -100) = Rs 1.2 Therefore, profit % = ( ) × 100 = 1.2%"}]',
