        1298,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"A person sells an article at a profit of 12% If he had purchased it for 12% less and sold it for Rs. 9 less, he would have gained 27%. What is the original cost price of the article?"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 3750"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 4500"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 4250"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 4000"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 3750"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option A Solution: Let the cost price of the article be 100x ⇒ Selling price = 112x (using multiplying factor) If he had purchased it for 12% less and sold it for Rs 9 less, Cost price = 100x × 0.88 ⇒ 88x ⇒ Selling price - Cost price = Profit ⇒ 112x - 9 - 88x = 88x × ⇒ 24x - 9 = ⇒ x(24 - 23.76) = 9 ⇒ x = ⇒ x = 37.5 ⇒ Original cost price = 100x = 3750"}]',
