    ),
    (
        1336,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Sanjay and Komal started a business with Rs. 15000 each. After 8 months Komal withdrew Rs. 10000. If at the end of a year there was a profit of Rs. 32000. What was the share of Sanjay in the profit ?"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 18000"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 18500"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 16500"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 16000"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Rs. 18000"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option A Solution: Sanjay''s investment for 1 months = 15000 x 12 = Rs. 180000 Komal''s investment for 1 months = 15000 x 8 + (15000 - 10000) x 4 = 120000 + 20000 = Rs. 140000 ∴ Ratio between the investment of Sanjay and Komal = 180000 : 140000 = 9 : 7 ∴ Sanjay''s profit = [9/(9 + 7)] x 32000 = Rs. 18000"}]',
        4,
