        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option B Solution: Let, B1 : B2 : B3 = 3x : 4x : 5x again B1 : B2 : B3 = 5y : 4y : 3y Since there is increase in no.of oranges in first two baskets only, it means the no. of oranges remains constant in the third basket Therefore, 5x = 3y Hence 3x : 4x : 5x => and 5y : 4y : 3y => 25x : 20x : 15x Therfore, increment in first basket = 16 Increment in second basket = 8 Thus, required ratio = 16/8 = 2:1"}]',
