        1379,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"An alloy A is formed by mixing gold and silver in the ratio 2 : 1. Another alloy B is formed by mixing silver and platinum in the ratio 3 : 4. An alloy C is obtained by mixing alloys A and B in a certain ratio such that the ratio of gold and platinum in alloy C is 5 : 6. Which of the following correctly represents the share of silver in alloy C."}]',
