        '[{"type":"text","value":"[MISSING_OPTION_TEXT]"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option D Solution: We have been given that alloy A contains gold and silver in the ratio 2 : 1. Let there be 21x units of A. So it will have 14x units of gold and 7x units of silver. Let there be 21y units of alloy B. So we have 9 units of silver and 12 units of platinum. Let these two be mixed to get the desired alloy. Hence, the total amount of gold in alloy C will be 14x and total amount of platinum will be 12y. We have been given that = ⇒ 84x = 60y ⇒ = Thus alloys A and B must have been mixed in the ratio 5 : 7 Thus, the share of silver in the final mixture = = ="}]',
