    (
        1436,
        '[{"type":"text","value":"A, B and C working separately can do a piece of work in 60, 120 and 80 days respectively. A and B started working, then after 20 days, A left the work and C joined them. In how much time do they completed the total work?"}]',
        '[[{"type":"text","value":"46"}],[{"type":"text","value":"43"}],[{"type":"text","value":"36"}],[{"type":"text","value":"44"}]]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"44"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option D Solution: Since, no. of days taken by A, B and C to complete the work alone is 60, 120 and days respectively, Hence total work = LCM of 60, 120 and 80 =240 units Thus, Efficiency of A = = 4 units Efficiency of B = = 2 units Efficiency of C = = 3 units Now, A and B worked together for 20 days, So total work done in 20 days = Efficiency of (A + B) × 20 = (4 + 2) × 20 = 120 units Work left to be completed = 240 - 120 = 120 units According to question, this work is completed by B and C together So, no. of days taken by B and C to complete the remaining work = Remaining work/Efficiency of (B + C) ⇒ = = 24 days Hence, total time taken by A, B and C to complete the work = 20 + 24 = 44 days"}]',
