        '[{"type":"text","value":"15 days"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option C Solution: Each person can complete the work in 15 days so, 3 of them together can complete the work in = 5 days I.e. each day, they can complete = 20% of work Now, manish can destroy the complete wall in 7 days so each day, he can destroy, = 14.28% of wall If all of them work together, (building and destroying) Total effective work each day = 20% - 14.28% = 5.72% of work each day Since on the last day, before Manish destroys the wall, the wall gets completed once, work will be done whole 20%. Hence, task that would be done simultaneously by masons and Manish = 100 - 20 = 80% No. of days to complete the 80% work = = 13.98 or 14 days Now, since on the last day the wall completes before Manish breaks it, hence total no. of days = 14 + 1 = 15 days"}]',
