        '[{"type":"text","value":"Rs 200"}]',
        '[{"type":"text","value":"Answer: Option C Solution: L.C.M of 40, 20, 30 = 120 Let there be 120 units of work to be finished Since, A can do 120 units of work in 40 days so, he does = 3 units per day Since, B can finish 120 units in 30 days so, he does = 4 units per day Since, C can finish 120 units in 20 days, he does = 6 units per day They worked together for 3 days So work done in 5 days = 3 × (3 + 6 + 4) = 13 × 3 = 39 units Remaining work = 120 - 39 = 81 Units of work done by A and C in one day = 3 + 6 = 9 Time taken by A and C = = 9 days Total units of work done by A = 3 × (9 + 3) = 36 units Total units of work done by B = 4 × 3 = 12 units Total units of work done by C = 6 × (9 + 3) = 72 units Share of B = × 2000 = Rs 200"}]',
